Requirements: 13   with obligations: 13

[task-01] The review injects an edit for each plausible defect it enumerates and runs
    the project's candidate tests against that edit. It must use what that run showed to
    decide which defect-and-test pairs are worth putting to a model, so that the model
    is asked far fewer of those questions than it is asked today.
    -> inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect  [functional/explicit]
       Inject an edit for each plausible defect it enumerates.
    -> run-candidate-tests-against-edit  [functional/explicit]
       Run the project's candidate tests against that edit.
    -> run-guided-pair-selection  [functional/explicit]
       Use what the candidate-test run showed to decide which defect-and-test pairs are
       worth putting to a model.
    -> reduce-model-questions  [functional/explicit]
       The review asks the model far fewer defect-and-test questions than it does today.

[task-02] Where at least one candidate test failed under an edit, a test that went on
    passing under the same edit is not put to the model. The tests that failed under it
    are still put to the model, because a test going red does not on its own say the
    named defect is what it caught.
    -> exclude-passing-tests-under-edit  [functional/explicit]
       A test that went on passing under the same edit is not put to the model when at
       least one candidate test failed under that edit.
    -> retain-failed-tests-in-model-input  [functional/explicit]
       The tests that failed under it are still put to the model.
    -> red-test-does-not-identify-defect  [invariant/explicit]
       A test going red does not by itself establish that the named defect is what it
       caught.

[task-03] Where no candidate test failed under an edit, every pair for that defect is
    put to the model, as is every pair for a defect no edit could be built for.
    -> every-pair-put-to-model-when-no-candidate-test-failed  [functional/explicit]
       Where no candidate test failed under an edit, every pair for that defect is put
       to the model.
    -> every-pair-for-unbuildable-defect  [functional/explicit]
       Every pair for a defect no edit could be built for is put to the model.

[task-04] A pair the review drops this way has not been decided, and must not read as
    though it had been. The review records, for each dropped pair, why it was dropped
    and which injection attempt the decision rests on. A dropped pair is not a
    demonstration that the test fails to catch the defect.
    -> must-not-read-as-though-it-had-been  [invariant/explicit]
       The requirement must not be read as though it had been.
    -> dropped-pair-drop-reason  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The review records, for each dropped pair, why it was dropped.
    -> injection-attempt-restatement  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Record which injection attempt the decision rests on.

[task-05] A run of the project's tests that would let the review drop pairs is worth
    doing on that ground alone.
    -> run-project-tests  [test_demand/explicit]
       Run the project's tests so the review can drop pairs.

[task-06] Dropping pairs can be turned off, so a review can still be run the way it runs
    today.
    -> dropping-pairs-can-be-turned-off  [functional/explicit]
       The review supports turning off dropping pairs.
    -> preserve-current-review-run-mode  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the ability to run a review the way it runs today.

[task-07] For each defect the stage was asked about, the report says how many of its
    pairs the run itself decided, how many were put to the model, and how many were
    dropped.
    -> report-says-how-many-pairs-run-decided  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many of its pairs the run itself decided.
    -> put-to-the-model-count  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many pairs were put to the model.
    -> dropped-pairs-count  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many pairs were dropped.

[constraint-01] Nothing about the edit, or about what the tests did under it, reaches
    the model.
    -> model-sees-no-edit-or-test-result  [invariant/explicit]
       Nothing about the edit or about what the tests did under it reaches the model.

[constraint-02] An edit nobody checked still settles nothing. A dropped pair reaches no
    evidence tier and yields no finding.
    -> unchecked-edit-settles-nothing  [invariant/explicit]
       An edit that was not separately checked does not settle the question of whether
       it makes the named defect true.
    -> dropped-pair-no-evidence-tier  [invariant/explicit]
       A dropped pair does not reach any evidence tier and does not yield a finding.

[exclusion-01] Checking whether an edit really makes its named defect true.
    -> no-edit-checking  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not add or perform checking whether an edit really makes its
       named defect true.

[exclusion-02] Building an edit, choosing the region it falls in, or deciding whether it
    is valid.
    -> no-edit-construction-or-validation  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not include building an edit, choosing the region it falls in, or
       deciding whether it is valid.

[exclusion-03] Which tests are candidates, and whether the project's tests can be run at
    all.
    -> exclude-test-selection-and-run-eligibility  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are candidates, and it does not alter
       whether the project's tests can be run at all.

[exclusion-04] Running the project's whole test suite.
    -> no-whole-suite-run  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not run the project's whole test suite.

